{"entryId":"1283","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1283:1","sourceSha256":"d55c2c572889de4a418715e1b9c2ad25e501400e7b65a6ae06f958b89d5564f9","englishSha256":"15bb526558fffc1e2f4e63087f6c32a3c4f71089ce1018a913afef6c5da06984","citations":[{"id":"1283:1:citation-01","he":[67,110],"en":[29,39],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_42b.2"},"reference":"Sukkah 42b:2","assessment":"The checked Rif explicitly has Rav Chiyya bar Abba, son of Rav Avya. It confirms the entire alternative patronymic, with a Rav title.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rif Sukkah 20b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Sukkah_20b.4"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sukkah 42b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_42b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1283:1:citation-02","he":[36,65],"en":[41,67],"target":{"entry":1395,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1395:1","assessment":"The exact internal Chanin dossier exists but does not settle the identification.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1395:1","target":{"entry":1395,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"1283:1:citation-03","he":[67,110],"en":[98,111],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Sukkah_20b.4"},"reference":"Rif Sukkah 20b:4","assessment":"The checked Rif explicitly has Rav Chiyya bar Abba, son of Rav Avya. It confirms the entire alternative patronymic, with a Rav title.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rif Sukkah 20b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Sukkah_20b.4"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sukkah 42b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_42b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[1,0],"holds":[{"raw":"אולי אחד הוא","reason":"The identity remains conjectural. The checked Sukkah and Rif preserve different names for the same law.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sukkah 42b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.s